So mammographies are obviously x-rays of your breasts

00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:27,150
to diagnose any irregularities and lesions

00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:30,710
that then would require getting a biopsy

00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:34,310
and to test for possible cancer.

00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:38,470
Thermography is a heat-sensitive instrument.

00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:43,150
So is thermography a viable substitute for mammography?

00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:47,710
In my opinion, yes, but they are testing different things.

00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:50,070
So you're gonna see different things

00:00:50,070 --> 00:00:55,070
in an x-ray of the breast versus thermography of the breast.

00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:58,590
I think thermography is best used for screening.

00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:01,070
Thermography is not a diagnostic tool.

00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:03,430
So you can't use it for diagnostic

00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:06,630
to nor can you really use mammography

00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:09,870
for diagnostic in the case of cancer.

00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:14,630
So the only way to diagnose cancer is with a biopsy.

00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:20,470
Thermography is gonna be much more sensitive to the mammography.

00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:25,070
You're gonna, you're going to catch things earlier

