Your, your diagnoses things to early,

00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:38,470
first of all incorrect, thermography is a diagnosing,

00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:41,830
but it is giving you an idea that there's something wrong.

00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:46,830
So if you have a regular thermography

00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:52,310
which I think if you're getting annual thermographies,

00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:55,190
if everything is clean up with thermography,

00:01:55,190 --> 00:01:57,630
thermographies are read by radiologists,

00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:00,550
medical radiologists, so it's not something that is like,

00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:05,310
it's not something that should even be considered like alternative.

00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:10,310
So I am not a fan of annual mammographies

00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:13,350
that radiation that you're putting in your breast

00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:17,310
on an annual basis could be cancer-causing to itself.

00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:20,710
There's no negatives of a thermography.

00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:22,230
It's taking a thermal picture.

00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:25,670
So there's zero in base of this on a thermography.

00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:29,190
So it's really like a perfect screening tool.

00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:33,030
So, but it is just a screening tool.

00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:36,990
So you use that and let's say something is positive on there

00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,150
then maybe you'll check that more regularly.

00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:40,710
Maybe you'll run two marker tests.

00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:43,150
Maybe you'll go to get an ultrasound done.

00:02:43,150 --> 00:02:45,270
It will pinpoint different things

00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:48,470
that maybe you want to look at and move forward with.

00:02:48,470 --> 00:02:50,710
So what is a good time to do a thermography?

00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:52,670
When you're healthy, it's a really good time

00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:54,590
to get it done in a thermography.

00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:56,550
Should everybody be doing a thermography?

00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,350
Yes, everybody should be doing a thermography.

00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:03,350
For sure, is thermography, this isn't the question,

00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:07,230
but is thermography misused?

00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:10,190
Why I think any test can be misused?

00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,230
I had a male once committed to,

00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:15,070
I had prostate cancer, but I had a thermography that didn't show up.

00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:17,390
It's not going to show up on thermography.

00:03:17,390 --> 00:03:20,150
So if thermography is going to show more surface things,

00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:25,150
I know, I'm licensed in thermography certified

00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:28,950
but that doesn't mean I necessarily agree

00:03:28,950 --> 00:03:33,270
that you're going to be able to see abdominal issues

00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:34,830
clearly with thermography.

00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:36,670
There's better tests to use.

00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:38,870
Thermography is great for surface things.

00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:42,390
Thermography could be helpful for aeropathy.

00:03:43,350 --> 00:03:46,230
Thermography could be helpful for a lot of things,

00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:50,190
but just like any test, like any blood test, anything else,

00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:54,070
a test is to give you clues as a diagnostician,

00:03:54,070 --> 00:03:55,510
to give you clues.

00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:57,510
Say, oh, well, there's something going on here.

00:03:57,510 --> 00:03:58,950
We need to dig a little bit deeper.

00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:01,270
We need to correlate that with other objective

00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:05,670
and subjective findings and subjective and objective tests

00:04:05,670 --> 00:04:10,390
in order to move forward with our working diagnosis.

00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:13,830
So part of being a good clinician is you're doing

00:04:13,830 --> 00:04:15,990
what's called differential diagnosis

00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:19,710
to come to a conclusion to a working diagnosis.

00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:23,990
And they'll say in medicine that you come to a final diagnosis,

00:04:23,990 --> 00:04:28,430
but in truth, in practice, everything is a working diagnosis.

00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:32,270
So that's what you use thermography and blood tests

00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:35,630
and CTs and MRIs and everything,

00:04:35,630 --> 00:04:38,350
to give you a working diagnosis to decide

00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:41,350
how you're going to move forward in a treatment plan.

00:04:41,350 --> 00:04:43,670
And then what you do through that treatment plan

00:04:43,670 --> 00:04:47,150
is you retest to make sure that you've actually

00:04:47,150 --> 00:04:50,510
accomplished something in through that working diagnosis.

00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:55,710
So this is what I see as a failure in our medical field today.

00:04:55,710 --> 00:04:59,750
So often do I talk to people that had blood tests done

00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:02,030
that abnormalities of that blood test.

00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:03,710
And it's like, what did your doctor do?

00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:04,310
Nothing.

00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:06,430
He didn't even talk to me about it.

00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:09,190
OK, you have anemia on this blood test

00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:11,430
that you had last September.

00:05:11,430 --> 00:05:13,390
He never did another blood test.

00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:15,150
I mean, this is just criminal.

00:05:15,150 --> 00:05:18,710
So he never even told the person that they had anemia.

00:05:18,710 --> 00:05:21,750
In order to even start a treatment procedure,

00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:24,270
why do you do the blood test in the first place?

00:05:24,270 --> 00:05:29,470
If you're not using that test to move towards a working diagnosis

00:05:29,470 --> 00:05:33,390
or give you clues that you should do other diagnostic procedures

00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:35,190
in order to help the patient.

00:05:35,190 --> 00:05:38,070
And then when you make the clinical decision

00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,710
to help the patient, then you rerun the tests

00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:45,150
that gave you that indication of what was abnormal

00:05:45,150 --> 00:05:49,670
is to see if you've actually collected it.

